<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech utility says plans bond issue.</title>
<headline>Czech utility says plans bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech electrical utility Elektrarny Opatovice a.s. on Thursday said it will propose issuing a 2.5 billion crown tranche of six year bonds at its annual general meeting next month.  </p>
<p>Pavel Hypus of the firm's financial department told Reuters that the coupon for the bonds will be set according to the actual situation on the market at the time of issue.</p>
<p>He added that funds from the bonds will be used for the company's investment programme and refinancing some of its current debt.</p>
<p>-- Dusan Bucanek, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
